Target: Meizu 21 Note, 5.15.119-android13-8-g6ff5097ee32a-ab1764665171 (qcom,kalama).
That kernel has CONFIG_MACVLAN=n and CONFIG_IP6_NF_NAT=n. masquerade for IPv6 is
already built in: CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_TARGET_MASQUERADE=y compiles xt_MASQUERADE,
which registers NFPROTO_IPV6 as well as NFPROTO_IPV4 in 5.15, and CONFIG_NF_NAT=y
provides nf_nat_masquerade_ipv6. CONFIG_IP6_NF_TARGET_MASQUERADE does not exist as a
separate 5.15 option (there is no ip6t_MASQUERADE.c). Only the IPv6 "nat" x_tables
template is therefore missing. CONFIG_NF_TABLES is not set, so no nftables unit is
added here.

The upstream files retain their original license notices. The local changes are:
- Replace the per-file module_init/module_exit entries with ds_nf_init_net515_* /
  ds_nf_exit_net515_* wrappers so one module can own both units and roll back in
  reverse order. Module metadata moved to main.c; the macvlan rtnl link alias is kept.
- Build with -DCONFIG_MACVLAN=1 so include/linux/if_macvlan.h provides the inlined
  accessors instead of the CONFIG_MACVLAN-less BUG() stubs.
- Restrict loading to the recorded device release or a 5.15.x linux,dummy-virt VM.

Nothing else is changed. Both units are the ordinary mainline modules: macvlan
registers its rtnl link kind and netdevice notifier, and ip6table_nat registers an
empty IPv6 "nat" table template. Module initialization installs no rules and creates
no links.

Regression entry point: tests/vm/run-net515.sh (requires a VM image with iproute2,
iptables-legacy and ip6tables; see docs/meizu21note-net-extras.md).
